<section class="tl-faq" id="opening-questions" aria-labelledby="tl-faq-heading">
  <div><p class="tl-eyebrow">A few things to know</p><h2 id="tl-faq-heading">Before we<br /><em>set the table.</em></h2><p>A first look should come with clear answers.</p></div>
  <div class="tl-faq-list">
    <details><summary>Can I order or reserve a bowl?</summary><p>No. The Table is in development. We are not accepting orders, payments, preorders or reservations. No opening date has been set.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What are you developing?</summary><p>Our first dish is the Southwest Harvest Bowl, a frozen bowl concept with rice, black beans, roasted sweet potatoes, peppers and onions, cilantro-lime sauce inside, and a separate dry pepita packet. The recipe is still being tested.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Is this a photograph of the finished meal?</summary><p>No. This is an owned concept illustration. It shows the intended composition, not a cooked meal, verified portion or final package. Actual meal photography can replace it after testing.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What about ingredients, allergens and nutrition?</summary><p>The complete ingredients, supplier subingredients, allergens, portion size and nutrition have not been verified. The planned components are not a final label or an allergen-safety claim.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Will pickup or delivery be available?</summary><p>We are planning toward serving Big Spring, Texas, and surrounding eligible areas. Pickup and delivery depend on operational and legal approval. Locations, service areas, fees, time windows and pricing are not confirmed.</p></details>
    <details><summary>How will I know when you're ready?</summary><p>Verified opening details will appear here. First come the recipe, packaging, safety review and fulfillment plan. There is no sign-up or waiting-list requirement to explore the bowl.</p></details>
  </div>
</section>
